## Data rules (apply to any topic)

- Public, keyless sources only. Cache every downloaded response to `data/cache/` — the loop
  must never re-fetch what it already has.
- Semantic Scholar Graph API / Crossref for citation verification (both keyless).
- NEVER fabricate, extrapolate, or hand-copy data values. If data cannot be fetched, record the blocker in TODO.md.

## Toolchain (you are OFFLINE — the harness handles all network)

- Python: `.venv/bin/python` — pandas, scipy, statsmodels, requests preinstalled (pinned
  in requirements.txt). Never pip install; there is no network in your sandbox.
- The model runner: `llama-completion -m data/models/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-q8_0.gguf
  -f <promptfile> -n <max_tokens> --temp 0 --seed 42 -c 9216 --no-display-prompt
  --simple-io` (llama.cpp; NOTE: llama-cli is interactive-only in this build — never
  use it in scripts). Call it via subprocess from analysis scripts.
- TWO-TIER PIPELINE (inference is expensive; aggregation is cheap):
  `make probes` runs `analysis/run_probes.py` (you create it) — generates all prompt
  files from seeded code, runs the model on each, writes raw outputs to `data/probes/`.
  Run it whenever you change the experiment grid. `make results` runs
